{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15409408","formula":"C₂₀H₃₁N","hill":"C20H31N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":31.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"Dehydroabietylamine","ru":"Лиламин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Leelamine (dehydroabietylamine) is a diterpene amine that has weak affinity for the cannabinoid receptors CB1 and CB2, as well as being an inhibitor of pyruvate dehydrogenase kinase. Optically active leelamine is also used as a chiral resolving agent for carboxylic acids. Leelamine has been shown to be effective against certain cancer cells, independent from its activity on CB receptors or PDK1 - it accumulates inside the acidic lysosomes leading to disruption of intracellular cholesterol transport, autophagy and endocytosis followed by cell death.","ru":"Лиламин (дегидроабетиламин) — вещество природного происхождения, дитерпеновый амин, имеющий слабую[уточнить] аффинность к каннабиноидным рецепторам CB1 и CB2. Ингибитор киназы пируватдегидрогеназы. Будучи оптически активным веществом, лиламин используется в качестве хирального агента для разделения карбоксиловых кислот."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":62034,"mass":285.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)C1=CC2=C(C=C1)[C@]3(CCC[C@@]([C@@H]3CC2)(C)CN)C","inchikey":"JVVXZOOGOGPDRZ-SLFFLAALSA-N","iupac":"[(1R,4aS,10aR)-1,4a-dimethyl-7-propan-2-yl-2,3,4,9,10,10a-hexahydrophenanthren-1-yl]methanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"62034","atoms":52,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.207,"y":1.489,"z":0.922,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.63,"y":0.464,"z":0.016,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.843,"y":-0.848,"z":-0.362,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.196,"y":0.365,"z":0.07,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.379,"y":-2.001,"z":0.531,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.605,"y":-0.874,"z":0.901,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.099,"y":1.648,"z":-0.809,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.897,"y":-2.155,"z":0.487,"el":